# HitoriShaders - HITORI KAKURENBO - option labels (English)
profile.LOW=Low
profile.MEDIUM=Medium
profile.HIGH=High
profile.ULTRA=Ultra
profile.comment=Quality preset. Medium is tuned for 60 fps on a mid-range GPU at 1080p. Low drops the reflections, the lamp shadows, the falling rain, the volumetric air and the light's shadows; High and Ultra trace finer reflections and smoother air.

screen.LIGHTS=Lights & TV
screen.LIGHTS.comment=The apartment's light sources: the CRT TV's static (the room's light after three), the lamps, the street lamp outside.
screen.RAIN=Rain & Reflections
screen.RAIN.comment=The rain: the wet street and its puddles, drops running down the windows, the bath water, the glossy floors and tiles.
screen.CCTV=Camera Feed
screen.CCTV.comment=What the fixed cameras' feeds look like in the camera app: IR night vision, noise, lens, lines and glitches.
screen.HANDLIGHT=Phone Light
screen.HANDLIGHT.comment=The phone's flashlight (and the dust in it).
screen.ATMOSPHERE=Air
screen.ATMOSPHERE.comment=The rain haze outside, the still dusty air of the rooms, the lights glowing in it.
screen.FEAR=Fear & Eyes
screen.FEAR.comment=What your heartbeat and the nearness of danger do to the picture; what you see with your eyes shut.
screen.POST=Image
screen.POST.comment=Film grain, vignette, chromatic aberration and bloom.
screen.SUN=Sun & Shadow
screen.SUN.comment=Sun and moon shadows outside the apartment's world (its sky is overcast and raining).

option.FLASH_REDUCTION=Flash Reduction
option.FLASH_REDUCTION.comment=For photosensitive players: a calmer TV flicker and lamp stutter, no heartbeat-pulsing vignette, no breathing image, almost no tearing on the camera feeds.
option.BRIGHTNESS=Brightness
option.BRIGHTNESS.comment=Overall brightness (also the camera feeds). Raise it if you cannot see anything (the horror gets a little weaker).

option.COLORED_LIGHT=Coloured Lights
option.COLORED_LIGHT.comment=Every light lights its surroundings in its own colour, with its own flicker and highlights on glossy surfaces: the TV's cold blue, the sodium orange, the laptop's white. Off: one warm block light.
option.LIGHT_STRENGTH=Lamp Brightness
option.LIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the apartment's lamps and the street lamp light the world.
option.TV_STRENGTH=TV Brightness
option.TV_STRENGTH.comment=How strongly the CRT TV's static lights the tatami room (and what leaks into the closet).
option.LIGHT_SHADOWS=Light Shadows
option.LIGHT_SHADOWS.comment=The low table, the cushions, the doll throw shadows from the TV and the nearest lamp (screen space). The closet's slit of light works either way.
option.LIGHT_FLICKER=Flicker
option.LIGHT_FLICKER.comment=The TV's static breathes and drops out, old tubes shimmer, the dying street lamp fades and restrikes, the lamps stutter when danger is near.
option.TV_STATIC=CRT Static
option.TV_STATIC.comment=The TV's screen shows real static: fine snow changing every frame, scanlines, a rolling bar. Off: only the texture.

option.REFLECTIONS=Reflections
option.REFLECTIONS.comment=Screen-space reflections: the street lamp in the wet street and the puddles, the bath water, the wet tiles, the old floor, the mirrors, the dead TV's glass.
option.SSR_STEPS=Reflection Quality
option.SSR_STEPS.comment=Steps per reflected ray. More reaches further and misses less, but is slower.
option.WET_SURFACES=Wet in the Rain
option.WET_SURFACES.comment=Everything under the open sky is wet: darker, glossy, with standing water in the dips.
option.RAIN_ON_GLASS=Rain on the Windows
option.RAIN_ON_GLASS.comment=Drops sit on the windows and the balcony doors and run down them in fits, leaving trails; they bend the street lamp's light into points.
option.RAIN_STREAKS=Falling Rain
option.RAIN_STREAKS.comment=The rain falling outside, seen where the street lamp and the vending machine light it.
option.WATER_RIPPLES=Rings on the Water
option.WATER_RIPPLES.comment=Rain falling into the puddles, drips falling into the full bathtub.

option.CCTV_NOISE=Feed Noise
option.CCTV_NOISE.comment=The camera's sensor noise. It grows the darker the room is (the camera turns its gain up).
option.CCTV_FISHEYE=Feed Fisheye
option.CCTV_FISHEYE.comment=The slight fisheye of an action camera's wide lens.
option.CCTV_SCANLINES=Feed Scanlines
option.CCTV_SCANLINES.comment=The feed's lines and a slow rolling bar.
option.CCTV_INTERLACE=Feed Interlacing
option.CCTV_INTERLACE.comment=Every other line comes from the previous field: whatever moves on the feed shows combed edges.
option.CCTV_GLITCH=Feed Glitches
option.CCTV_GLITCH.comment=The feed tears and its colours split while the doll or something else is on the picture, and when danger is near.
option.APPARITION_HAZE=Apparition Haze
option.APPARITION_HAZE.comment=On a camera feed the air wavers round what only the camera sees.

option.BEAM_STRENGTH=Phone Light Brightness
option.BEAM_STRENGTH.comment=How brightly the phone's flashlight lights the world.
option.BEAM_FOG=Visible Light Cone
option.BEAM_FOG.comment=How strongly the phone's light shows in the dusty air. 0 turns the visible cone off.
option.BEAM_SAMPLES=Light Cone Quality
option.BEAM_SAMPLES.comment=Samples per pixel for the visible cone. More is smoother but slower.
option.BEAM_SHADOWS=Hand Light Shadows
option.BEAM_SHADOWS.comment=Things throw shadows in the phone's light and the lighter's (screen space).
option.DUST_MOTES=Dust in the Light
option.DUST_MOTES.comment=Specks of dust floating in the phone's light (fine droplets outside).

option.FOG_DENSITY=Air Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=How thick the rain haze and the dust are. Lower it to see further.
option.FOG_NOISE=Drifting Rain Haze
option.FOG_NOISE.comment=The haze is uneven and drifts in veils with the rain. Off: smooth (faster).
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG=Volumetric Air
option.VOLUMETRIC_FOG.comment=The air is marched through: the street lamp's halo in the rain, the TV's glow in the dust. Off: a cheaper estimate.
option.VOLUMETRIC_SAMPLES=Air Quality
option.VOLUMETRIC_SAMPLES.comment=Samples per pixel for the air. More is smoother but slower.

option.FEAR_EFFECTS=Fear Effects
option.FEAR_EFFECTS.comment=Strength of the heartbeat vignette, tunnel vision, colour fringes, breathing image and double vision.
option.PAREIDOLIA=Faces in the Dark
option.PAREIDOLIA.comment=At very high fear, something like faces seems to form in the darkness at the edge of your vision.
option.PHOSPHENES=Phosphenes
option.PHOSPHENES.comment=With your eyes shut, faint colours drift in the black.

option.SHADOWS=Shadows
option.SHADOWS.comment=Shadows cast by the sun and the moon (outside the apartment's world).
option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Higher gives finer sun shadows but is slower. (The apartment's world uses its own small light map.)
option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far the sun shadows reach.
option.SHADOW_FILTER=Shadow Quality
option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment=Number of samples that soften the shadow edges.
value.SHADOW_FILTER.1=Low (4)
value.SHADOW_FILTER.2=Medium (8)
value.SHADOW_FILTER.3=High (12)
option.WAVING_PLANTS=Swaying Plants
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=Leaves and plants stir in the wind and the rain.

option.FILM_GRAIN=Film Grain
option.FILM_GRAIN.comment=Grain noise. Stronger with fear and danger.
option.VIGNETTE=Vignette
option.VIGNETTE.comment=Darkens the corners. It closes in with fear and beats with your heart; tighter in the closet.
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION=Chromatic Aberration
option.CHROMATIC_ABERRATION.comment=Colour fringes at the edges. Stronger at high fear and in danger.
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=Soft glow round the TV's screen, the lamps, the slit of light; the camera feeds bloom more.
